    "title": "Victor Wembanyama Pulls Off Another Unreal Play That Shouldn't Even Be Physically Possible [VIDEO] - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kenny Nosay ,\n14 minutes ago\nhttps://www.totalprosports.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Victor-Wembanyama-800x450.jpg Victor Wembanyama (Image Credits: @NBA/X) Whether it’s preseason or the regular season, Spurs big man Victor Wembanyama has dazzling plays that make us scratch our heads. After spending his offseason training with Hakeem Olajuwon and Kevin Garnett , Wembanyama, who is entering his third year in the NBA, is projected to become one of the best players in the 2025-2026 season.\nOfficially listed at 7’5”, Wemby can do it all in the court. He can dribble like a guard, shoot it from distance, and is one of the best finishers above the rim. Truth be told, nobody can stop him one-on-one.\nWe’ve seen plenty of Wembanyama highlights since he came into the league a couple of years ago. However, his recent play against the Dallas Mavericks on opening night has left everybody speechless. The clip has been shared on X by the NBA’s official account.\nRecognizing that Wemby was running towards the rim, Spurs guard Stephon Castle threw a high lob pass, hoping that his teammate would catch it. Wembanyama then proceeded to twist in the middle of the air and finish the play with a reverse jam.\nIs Victor Wembanyama Actually Taller Than His Listed Height? Victor Wemb anyama (Image Credits: Imagn) When Wemby was drafted by the Spurs in 2023, they listed him at 7’4”. By the time he stepped foot on an NBA court, it was obvious that he was taller than his peers. Even opponents listed at 7 feet appear visibly smaller when guarding Wemby.\nFormer NBA player Boban Marjanovic, who is 7’4” himself, has reiterated that he looked up when Wemby was beside him . That should be a clear indicator that the 21-year-old Spurs star might be closer to 7’7” in real life. Now, if he avoids any major injuries in the future, then the Spurs will have the chance to build another dynasty, and Victor Wembanyama will be the center of it all.\nThe post originally published on .",
